{# A value to copy: a readonly box, and a button that copies what it holds.

   `copyField(id, label, value)` emits

     <label class="sr-only" for="id">label</label>
     <div class="join w-full">
       <input id="id" type="text" value="value" readonly class="input input-sm join-item w-full" />
       <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm join-item" data-copy="id" hidden>Copy</button>
     </div>

   The box selects and copies like any other text, so the value can be taken
   with no script at all. The button is `hidden` until `static/copy.js` finds
   the clipboard API and reveals it: a button that did nothing without
   JavaScript would be worse than none. The label is read by a screen reader
   and not drawn, for a table cell whose column already says what it is.
   Label and value are escaped. #}

{% macro copyField(id, label, value) -%}
<label class="sr-only" for="{{ id }}">{{ label }}</label>
<div class="join w-full">
  <input id="{{ id }}" type="text" value="{{ value }}" readonly class="input input-sm join-item w-full min-w-48" />
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm join-item" data-copy="{{ id }}" hidden>Copy</button>
</div>
{%- endmacro %}
